    "problemStatement": "**This is the hard version of the problem. The only difference between this and the easy version is that here, 1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq Q \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105.\n\nThis problem is worth 505050 points.**\n\nYou're given a permutation†^\\dagger† PPP of the integers 111 to NNN.\n\nThere is beauty in order, so you'll only be satisfied if PPP is sorted in ascending order, i.e. Pi&lt;Pi+1P_i \\lt P_{i+1}Pi​&lt;Pi+1​ for each index iii from 111 to N−1N-1N−1.\n\nTo achieve this, you can perform the following operation:\n\n\nChoose an index iii such that Pi=iP_i = iPi​=i, and\n\nFreely rearrange the elements P1,P2,…,Pi−1P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_{i-1}P1​,P2​,…,Pi−1​ among positions 1,2,…,i−11, 2, \\ldots, i-11,2,…,i−1.\nFreely rearrange the elements Pi+1,Pi+2,…,PNP_{i+1}, P_{i+2}, \\ldots, P_{N}Pi+1​,Pi+2​,…,PN​ among positions i+1,i+2,…,Ni+1, i+2, \\ldots, Ni+1,i+2,…,N.\n\n\nDefine f(P)f(P)f(P) to be the minimum number of such operations needed to sort PPP in ascending order.\n\nIf it's impossible to sort PPP using these operations, f(P)=−1f(P) = -1f(P)=−1 instead.\n\nYou are also given QQQ updates to the permutation PPP.\n\nEach update gives you two integers xxx and yyy, and you must perform the operation swap(Px,Py)\\text{swap}(P_x, P_y)swap(Px​,Py​).\n\nYour task is to compute the value of f(P)f(P)f(P) before any updates are made, and also after each update.\n\n†^\\dagger† A permutation of the integers 111 to NNN is an array of length NNN that contains every integer from 111 to NNN. For instance, [1],[2,1],[4,2,1,3][1], [2, 1], [4, 2, 1, 3][1],[2,1],[4,2,1,3] are examples of permutations, while [1,1,3][1, 1, 3][1,1,3] and [2,4,5,1][2, 4, 5, 1][2,4,5,1] are not.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ – the length of the permutation and the number of updates.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​, describing the initial permutation.\nThe next QQQ lines describe the updates. The iii-th of them contains two space-separated integers xix_ixi​ and yiy_iyi​, denoting the indices whose values must be swapped in the iii-th operation.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line Q+1Q+1Q+1 space-separated integers: the value of f(P)f(P)f(P) before any updates, and also after each update.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅105\\red{1 \\leq Q \\leq 2\\cdot 10^5}1≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "PPP is a permutation of the integers 111 to NNN.",
      "1≤xi,yi≤N1 \\leq x_i, y_i \\leq N1≤xi​,yi​≤N and xi≠yix_i \\neq y_ixi​=yi​",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of QQQ over all test cases both won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
